# Line-ending policy (Sprint 61 Task 0, approved by Harold 2026-08-16).
#
# WHY: with no .gitattributes, Git's autocrlf on Windows converted line endings
# per-checkout, so every commit emitted "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings
# and files written LF by tooling showed as fully-changed diffs. Normalizing in
# the repository removes that entire class of noise.
#
# The repo stores LF and checks out LF. LF is also what the Flutter/Dart
# ecosystem and the ubuntu CI runners expect.
* text=auto eol=lf

# EXCEPTIONS -- Windows-native script types stay CRLF:
#  - .bat / .cmd: cmd.exe has documented parsing edge cases with LF line
#    endings (notably around labels used by goto), so CRLF is the safe default.
#  - .ps1: PowerShell itself handles LF fine, but Authenticode signature blocks
#    assume CRLF, so a signed script would break. Pinned pre-emptively.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary assets -- never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.msix binary
*.appx binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.xlsx binary
*.db binary
